WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.535
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show,"
everyone.

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:03.969
During what continues to be
a very turbulent time,

00:00:03.969 --> 00:00:06.672
I just want to say
to everyone out there protesting

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:09.141
or people going back to work
during quarantine,

00:00:09.141 --> 00:00:11.477
please stay safe.

00:00:11.477 --> 00:00:13.613
And we appreciate you.

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:15.982
We have a great show tonight.

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:19.052
The co-hosts of "Queer Eye"
are on the show tonight.

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:22.521
And their new season
just came out on Netflix.

00:00:22.521 --> 00:00:26.792
And we saw episode one,
and it is just great.

00:00:26.792 --> 00:00:28.995
They are just -- it's --
it's almost --

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:32.498
it's comforting,
but it's heartbreaking.

00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:34.533
It's beautiful.
It's great.

00:00:34.533 --> 00:00:36.602
And that was only
halfway through it.

00:00:36.602 --> 00:00:38.671
-Oh, yeah.
-Yeah, even to the end

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.306
is just -- yeah.
It's fantastic.

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:43.409
But we love all of those guys,
so they're on the show tonight,

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:46.178
as well as Christian Slater,

00:00:46.178 --> 00:00:49.516
who has a new show on USA,
Tuesdays, at 10:00.

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:50.883
And, honey, you'll like it.

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:52.418
It's, like, season two
of "Dirty John."

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:53.819
It's a real --
-Oh, I'm in.

00:00:53.819 --> 00:00:57.957
-Yep.
And then our music tonight,

00:00:57.957 --> 00:00:59.091
she's unbelievable.

00:00:59.091 --> 00:01:02.095
And Sia is on the show tonight.

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:03.430
-Oh.
-Yeah.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.798
She has a motion picture
called "Music,"

00:01:05.798 --> 00:01:07.466
and the song's called
"Together."

00:01:07.466 --> 00:01:10.903
And Sia is one -- I wish --
you know, I miss seeing

00:01:10.903 --> 00:01:13.739
these people and being
in front of these singers.

00:01:13.739 --> 00:01:15.975
'Cause it's people
like Sia that --

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:18.678
And musicians will know
what I'm talking about --

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:20.279
She almost doesn't need
a microphone

00:01:20.279 --> 00:01:21.613
when she's performing.

00:01:21.613 --> 00:01:25.084
She's so good and, like,
projecting, and it's like, wow!

00:01:25.084 --> 00:01:26.485
It's powerful.

00:01:26.485 --> 00:01:28.721
And I'm always like, "Wow.
Were you even using the mic?"

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.690
'Cause she fills up
the whole room.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:34.527
And I remember
even her doing "Chandelier,"

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:35.761
I want to say, and I was like,

00:01:35.761 --> 00:01:36.996
"You're not gonna
hit those notes."

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:39.032
It was like --
[ Whistling ]

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:41.667
I can't even whistle it,
what she was singing.

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:43.603
♪ Chandelier ♪
And she hit all the notes,

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:45.805
and I was like, "Ah!"
She is just amazing.

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:47.473
So, what a great show tonight.

00:01:47.473 --> 00:01:49.876
And thank you so much, again,
for watching.

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:51.811
Let's get to some news.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:55.581
Well, you guys, it's another
rough week for President Trump.

00:01:55.581 --> 00:01:57.049
Though at this point,
I can just say,

00:01:57.049 --> 00:02:00.220
"Well, you guys, it's another
week for President Trump."

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.454
CNN just released
a new poll yesterday,

00:02:02.454 --> 00:02:05.024
and it doesn't look too good
for the President.

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:06.993
-President Trump's
approval rating is the lowest

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.928
it's been since January
of last year.

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:10.529
That's according
to a new CNN poll

00:02:10.529 --> 00:02:13.466
that shows the President
slipping amid a chaotic week.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:16.269
Only 38% approve
of the job he is doing.

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:19.005
That is down 7 points
since just last month.

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:20.739
-Ouch.
Right now, the only thing

00:02:20.739 --> 00:02:22.241
lower than Trump's
approval rating

00:02:22.241 --> 00:02:24.477
is his underground bunker.

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:27.747
38%, to put that in perspective,
more people approved

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:31.750
of Lay's cappuccino-flavored
potato chips.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:35.087
Cappuccino-flavored
potato chips.

00:02:35.087 --> 00:02:39.992
Incidentally, 38% is
the same ratio of chips to air

00:02:39.992 --> 00:02:42.895
in every bag
of Lay's potato chips.

00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:44.931
It's bad. Right now,
even the "New York Times"

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:47.834
op-ed section has more fans.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:50.569
[ Chuckles ]

00:02:50.569 --> 00:02:51.804
You know
how I know things are bad?

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:55.374
Earlier today, Don Jr.
changed his name to Eric.

00:02:55.374 --> 00:02:58.544
[ Laughs ]

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:00.213
And now Trump
wants to improve his numbers

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:04.150
by getting his campaign team
from 2016 back together.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:07.587
Trump was like, "We can do it.
They're all out of prison now.

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:11.424
So..."

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:12.959
Speaking of Trump's campaign,

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:15.728
it looks like he's ready
to get back out on the road.

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:17.129
-And now the President
is planning

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:18.831
to get back out on the trail.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.800
His campaign says
they're looking to resume

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.035
those big rallies
in the next two weeks,

00:03:23.035 --> 00:03:25.938
despite concerns
about the pandemic.

00:03:25.938 --> 00:03:28.474
-Don't worry.
Just to be safe,

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:31.644
everyone gets injected with
bleach on the way in and out.

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.379
So...

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:35.648
Actually, Trump said that
they're being smart.

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:37.250
He was like,
"When the rally ends,

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.818
everyone will have
to stay in the arena

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:40.486
for two weeks of quarantine."

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:43.256
So, that's fair, right?

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:44.924
Meanwhile, just when it seemed
like things

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:46.358
couldn't get any more upsetting,

00:03:46.358 --> 00:03:48.528
Trump took to Twitter
this morning

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:50.062
to offer a conspiracy theory

00:03:50.062 --> 00:03:52.531
of the police-brutality incident
in Buffalo.

00:03:52.531 --> 00:03:56.435
He said that the 75-year-old man
who was shoved by the police

00:03:56.435 --> 00:03:59.338
could be an ANTIFA provocateur.

00:03:59.338 --> 00:04:03.176
And, "I watched.
He fell harder than was pushed.

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:04.543
Could be a setup?"

00:04:04.543 --> 00:04:07.580
Yeah, it's pretty interesting
that this guy

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:11.784
is giving a lesson on gravity,
from a man who stands like this.

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:21.127
It's almost like he's, like,
free falling,

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:23.028
like one of those
flying squirrel guys.

00:04:23.028 --> 00:04:26.432
♪ Defying gravity ♪

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:28.534
Um...

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:31.336
After receiving criticism from
both Democrats and Republicans

00:04:31.336 --> 00:04:35.241
for that exact tweet,
Trump followed up by tweeting,

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:37.409
"Make America great again."

00:04:37.409 --> 00:04:41.547
'Cause when the new stuff bombs,
you got to go with the hits.

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:42.981
Well, I saw
that Daniel Radcliffe

00:04:42.981 --> 00:04:45.217
released a statement condemning
J.K. Rowling's

00:04:45.217 --> 00:04:47.753
controversial tweets
about trans people.

00:04:47.753 --> 00:04:49.789
Many people have been surprised
about her views,

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:51.757
but I don't know.
If you go back and read

00:04:51.757 --> 00:04:54.727
the "Harry Potter" books,
it kind of makes sense.

00:04:54.727 --> 00:04:57.095
There's a character
that I forgot totally about.

00:04:57.095 --> 00:05:02.101
There's Hermione, Ron, Harry,
and, of course,

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:06.239
there was the fourth friend
that I forgot called Whimpleton.

00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:07.540
I totally --

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:10.576
Well, here's a couple excerpts
from the audiobooks.

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:12.611
Should make more sense.
Listen.

00:05:12.611 --> 00:05:14.479
♪♪

00:05:14.479 --> 00:05:15.915
-"We have to stop
Professor Snape

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:17.283
from getting
the Babbling Thwoggit!"

00:05:17.283 --> 00:05:18.450
exclaimed Harry.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:20.419
"Grab your wands!"
cried Hermione.

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:22.221
"I'm just gonna say it.
I'm not totally sold

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:24.757
on this whole 'trans' thing,"
said Whimpleton.

00:05:24.757 --> 00:05:28.327
"Not the time, Whimpleton!"
yelled Harry. "Wow!"

00:05:28.327 --> 00:05:30.329
"Use the Portkey
to get to the Jackalion!"

00:05:30.329 --> 00:05:31.564
declared Hermione.

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:33.899
"What kind of creature is that?"
inquired Ron.

00:05:33.899 --> 00:05:36.636
"Does it have claws and sharp
teeth?" queried Harry.

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:38.170
"And is it a boy or a girl?

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:41.607
It has to be one, not neither
or both," said Whimpleton.

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:44.644
"Whimpleton, literally no one
asked for your opinion here!"

00:05:44.644 --> 00:05:46.779
shouted the group.

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:49.382
"We've only found 16 of the
cursed Nobbilynooks!"

00:05:49.382 --> 00:05:51.084
Ron gasped.

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:52.451
"We have to hurry!"
bellowed Harry.

00:05:52.451 --> 00:05:54.587
"But wait!"
Whimpleton halted.

00:05:54.587 --> 00:05:56.856
"Can I just say, the thing
about menstruation is --"

00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:58.423
He never got
to finish his sentence,

00:05:58.423 --> 00:06:00.126
as Hermione pulled out her wand

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:02.394
and transfigured him
into a tea cozy

00:06:02.394 --> 00:06:06.032
And at last,
Whimpleton was useful.

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:08.468
But people are thanking
Daniel Radcliffe

00:06:08.468 --> 00:06:11.404
for speaking out against
J.K. Rowling's tweets.

00:06:11.404 --> 00:06:13.406
It's an easy issue to get wrong,

00:06:13.406 --> 00:06:15.208
so just so everyone's
on the same page,

00:06:15.208 --> 00:06:17.076
here's a complete list
of all the things

00:06:17.076 --> 00:06:20.346
people want to hear
J.K. Rowling's take on.

00:06:20.346 --> 00:06:22.882
♪♪

00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:24.183
-Wizards.

00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:26.052
♪♪

